 This install applies to "Road Rash" © 1992 Electronic Arts - 2 disks.

 This install requires WHDLoad 17.2 or newer to be in the path. It can be found in the
 WHDLoad package.

 The installed program requires 1 MB ChipMem and 1 MB OtherMem.
 It can be quit by pressing num '*' (key can be changed with Tooltype "QuitKey=").

 If you have problems with this installation please try and get a newer
 version of this package from the WHDLoad WWW-Page. If that doesn't help try
 some Tooltypes like NOCACHE, NOAUTOVEC, NOVBRMOVE, NOMMU, PAL or NTSC. If
 that also fails, please inform the author via the Bug-Report-Form which
 can be accessed on the WHDLoad WWW-Page or create a mantis issue directly
 at http://mantis.whdload.de

 For the full WHDLoad package, other installs and updates refer to:
	http://www.whdload.de/
 or	aminet:dev/misc/whdload#?
 and	aminet:game/patch/

 Version 2.1 beta (20.10.2026):
 - fixed idle joystick steering recentring and keyboard/CD32 pause handling
 - wait for screen DMA before loading files, fixing the uncached 68030 crash
 - single boolean option "Enhanced framerate" (CUSTOM2=1); off by default
 - on 68020+ with Fast RAM, advances simulation in 20 ms PAL steps and renders
   completed frames as fast as possible while retaining vsync
 - enhanced path enables CPU caches automatically unless NoCache is specified
 - enhanced path relocates the loader, title, intro, main program, menus and
   CPU data into optional public RAM, using Fast RAM when available; reserves
   388 KB including stacks, CPU image descriptions and music patterns
 - movement, collision, AI and acceleration code runs from Fast RAM on the
   enhanced path
 - uncached 68020 lane scanning also runs from Fast RAM on the enhanced path
 - enhanced lane occupancy uses actor widths instead of leftover rendering
   values; opponent paths and collision outcomes can differ from the original
 - raster edge generation runs from Fast RAM on the enhanced path
 - shared collision/pose scratch words use Fast RAM on the enhanced path
 - collision checks avoid redundant writes to already-clear actor flags
 - simulation derives rider lean during pose selection, avoiding a second
   traversal of the actor list
 - calibrates one-field displacement to the original four-field movement
   convention without changing acceleration or backdating controller input
 - normalizes road movement for 50 Hz simulation, retaining fractional
   motion and resetting it across crashes, actor reuse and new races
 - collision checks skip road-width and edge drawing calculations; rendering
   still builds the complete road geometry
 - 68040/68060 reuse rendered road geometry for the next simulation tick
   on the enhanced path, avoiding a redundant rebuild
 - enhanced path uses a 16 KB CPU stack in optional Fast RAM; retains the
   original stack if the optional allocation is unavailable or unsuitable
 - predicts the displayed rider heading through the measured render interval
   to reduce visible steering lag without changing simulation or collisions
 - heading prediction follows recent motion, retaining a short average when
   integer heading repeats during a continuing turn
 - no added frame limiter or delayed interpolation; slow frames catch up the
   required simulation steps before rendering
 - CUSTOM2=0 (or omitted), 68000 and unsupported memory configurations retain
   original timing and rendering
 - input and loading fixes remain active with Enhanced framerate disabled

 Version 2.0 (18.08.2019) done by JOTD:
 - adapted to whdload v17
 - joypad support (issue #0003626)
 - when joypad is detected, game control text is adapted. Function
   keys become joypad buttons in the game messages.
 - ability to enter some preset passwords at startup
 - ability to enter user defined password with CUSTOM tooltype   
 - arrows mapped to joystick directions (issue #0002670)
 - enter names/passwords with joypad (no need for keyboard anymore)
 - source code included
 
 Version 1.3 (2002):
 - reworked install script. Files are now in the "data" directory,
 - manual included
 - added a ton of icons
  
 Version 1.2:
 - fixed remaining disk access
 
 Version 1.1:
 - fixed delay to see the map

 Version 1.0 (1997):
 
 - Full run from HD using WHDLoad
 - Memory patch to avoid to use 32 bit fast memory
 - Password protection removed (no more protection screen)
 

CD32 controls - menu:

F1 - RW/reverse:
F2 - FF/forward: 
F3 - Blue: enter password / select bike
F4 - Green: control method 1
F5 - Yellow: control method 2

To select a letter to input, use reverse & forward. This acts like
Earok "virtual keyboard": enters the letter then performs a cursor left
To select this letter, just use joystick right.

CD32 controls - game:

Space - PLAY: pause
F10 - reverse+forward: quit current game

Custom password:

The format matters: 5 chars - 2 spaces - 10 chars - 2 spaces - 5 chars
Ex: whdload roadrash.slave preload custom="00000  01420019G5  457VO"

There are 2 spaces above, regardless of your html viewer displays, like:

whdload roadrash.slave preload custom="00000<space><space>01420019G5<space><space>457VO"

